  "description": "TypeScript typecheck, lint, format, example-README, docs export-map, unit and coverage suites plus the Node engines floor and Lambda runtime deprecation checks, and a clean-consumer install of the packed tarball into an empty project exercised through a real SSR render and SSG build, under each supported Node major on Linux arm64 (oldest 22, middle 24, newest 26), which is the architecture each proof profile really runs. Linux/x64 is no longer proven anywhere: user-mode x86_64 emulation crashes Go-built binaries (esbuild aborts with 'found bad pointer in Go heap') on the producing host, so the historical GitHub runner's architecture cannot be recorded as covered. The Node-major floor is the claim these profiles carry.",
